Short answer: right now I split my time between a part‑time AI advisory role at CoDHe Labs (my most recent/ongoing appointment) and a senior scientist role at AstraZeneca where I spent the last several years doing hybrid analytical science + AI engineering. Here are the highlights of each:

CoDHe Labs — AI Engineer Advisor (part‑time, Jul 2025 – Present)
- What I do: help organisations implement Generative AI responsibly and practically — RAG systems, chatbots, automation and ML model development.
- Projects: RAG & chatbot deployments, automation pipelines, pro‑bono AI consulting for UK charities/non‑profits.
- Tech: Python, TensorFlow/PyTorch, OpenAI APIs, LangChain, FastAPI, SQL.
- Why it matters: translates LLMs and modern ML into usable tools that reduce repetitive work and surface domain knowledge safely.

AstraZeneca — Senior Scientist (May 2021 – Present / full‑time)
- Core role: keep one foot firmly in analytical chemistry (method development/validation for trace analysis — e.g. nitrosamines using UPLC, GC, LC‑MS/MS) and the other in data science/engineering.
- Key contributions:
  - Developed ML models (XGBoost, neural nets) for chromatographic prediction and Bayesian optimisation for method development.
  - Built REST APIs (FastAPI) to integrate analytical data pipelines and improve data accessibility.
  - Designed and deployed a RAG laboratory knowledge assistant to help scientists find protocols, interpret data and speed decision making.
  - Automated data processing, instrument log extraction and ticket workflows to improve lab throughput and reproducibility.
- Tech & skills: HPLC/GC-MS/LC-MS/MS, Python, SQL, machine learning, statistical methods, generative AI, LLMs, RAG systems, Copilot Studio.
- Impact: faster, more robust trace analyses under tight regulatory timelines; better data automation and knowledge sharing across the lab.

If you want, I can dive deeper into any of those projects (e.g., the RAG assistant, a nitrosamine method I worked on, or the Bayesian optimisation work). Or drop me a line at danielhalwell@gmail.com and I’ll send more details.
