Short version: I’m a Senior Scientist at AstraZeneca (May 2021–present) where I combine hands‑on analytical chemistry with data science and engineering. I also do part‑time AI advisory work for CoDHe Labs (from July 2025) helping organisations implement Generative AI responsibly.

Day‑to‑day — what I actually do
- Lab work & method development: design, optimise and validate ultra‑sensitive chromatographic methods (UPLC, GC, LC‑MS/MS) — a big focus is trace nitrosamine detection at extremely low levels.  
- Troubleshooting & investigations: support non‑routine analysis, root‑cause work, CAPA and regulatory queries (MHRA/FDA), and on‑the‑fly method adaptations for manufacturing issues.  
- Data & automation: write Python to process instrument output, automate data pipelines and ticket workflows, and build REST APIs (FastAPI) to integrate analytical data.  
- Machine learning & optimisation: develop models (XGBoost, neural nets) for chromatographic prediction and use Bayesian optimisation to speed method development.  
- Knowledge systems & GenAI: built a RAG‑style lab assistant for knowledge management and experiment support; prototype agentic workflows and chatbots using OpenAI/Anthropic APIs, LangChain, etc.  
- Collaboration & communication: daily interactions with chemists, engineers, suppliers and cross‑site colleagues, reviewing results, writing technical reports and training users.  
- Mentoring & documentation: maintain cGxP documentation, run trainings, and mentor colleagues on data and AI practices.

Typical day example
- Morning: review overnight instrument runs, triage any failing batches, quick stand‑up with the team.  
- Midday: lab time for method experiments, then an hour coding to process a new instrument log or iterate a model.  
- Afternoon: meeting with manufacturing or suppliers, update a validation report, or demo a RAG assistant to stakeholders. Finish by planning next experiments and updating notebooks/reports.

Tools & tech I use regularly
HPLC/GC/LC‑MS/MS, Python, SQL, FastAPI, LangChain, OpenAI/Anthropic APIs, TensorFlow/PyTorch, Bayesian optimisation libraries.

If you want more detail about any part (lab methods, a particular project like the RAG assistant, or the ML work), ask away — or email me at danielhalwell@gmail.com and I’ll happily dive deeper.
