Current role snapshot
- Senior Scientist, AstraZeneca (May 2021 – present). I sit at the intersection of analytical chemistry and data engineering: continuing hands‑on trace analytical work (especially nitrosamine risk investigations) while building automation, ML and AI solutions to speed up and improve lab science.
- I also do part‑time AI advisory work for CoDHe Labs (since July 2025), helping organisations implement responsible generative AI (RAG systems, chatbots, automation).

What I do day‑to‑day
- Analytical method development & validation: design and validate ultra‑sensitive methods (UPLC/HPLC, GC, LC‑MS/MS) for trace analytes such as nitrosamines — from sample prep through data review and reporting.
- Hands‑on instrument work: run and troubleshoot LC/GC/MS instruments, interpret chromatographic and spectral data.
- Automation & data engineering: write Python to clean, visualise and pipeline instrument data; build REST APIs (FastAPI) to integrate lab data sources.
- ML & optimisation: develop ML models (XGBoost, neural nets) for chromatographic prediction, and use Bayesian optimisation to speed method development.
- Knowledge systems: build and maintain RAG/chatbot assistants and knowledge management tools for lab users.
- Investigations & compliance support: lead or support investigations, root cause analysis, CAPA activities and prepare technical documentation for inspections (MHRA, FDA).
- Cross‑functional collaboration: work with manufacturing, suppliers, microbiologists and engineers to solve urgent problems and transfer methods; occasionally travel for training or troubleshooting.
- Mentoring & reporting: write technical reports, set acceptance criteria, mentor colleagues and participate in project planning.

A typical day (example)
- Morning: triage tickets, check overnight runs and QC results, quick stand‑up.
- Midday: instrument runs and data reviewing; write or update method documents.
- Afternoon: coding session (automation/analysis model), meetings with stakeholders (manufacturing/suppliers), prepare reports or training materials.
- End of day: push code/analyses, update project trackers, plan next steps.

Tech I use regularly
- Lab: HPLC/UPLC, GC, GC‑MS, LC‑MS/MS
- Code & infra: Python, SQL, FastAPI, LangChain, OpenAI/Anthropic APIs
- ML/statistics: XGBoost, neural networks, Bayesian optimisation
- Other: RAG systems, data visualisation and reporting tools

Impact highlights
- Built ML models for chromatographic prediction and Bayesian optimisation workflows to accelerate method development.
- Built REST APIs and a RAG lab assistant to improve data access and knowledge sharing across teams.

If you want more detail about any part — e.g., the nitrosamine methods, the RAG assistant, or a day where things went sideways and what we did — ask away or drop me a line at danielhalwell@gmail.com.
